# ADT multi-entry union declaration: [type [let a] Ok: [value: a] Error: [msg: String]]
# registers a parameterized Union type alias with two NominalVariant constructors.
# At runtime, the type dict contains the constructor functions Ok and Error.
# Calling Ok with value: integer and Error with msg: string both succeed.
[
  Result: [type [let a] Ok: [value: a] Error: [msg: String]]
  ok-val:  [Result.Ok value: 42]
  err-val: [Result.Error msg: "something went wrong"]
]
=== out
Dict({"Result": Dict({"Ok": Function(value), "Error": Function(msg)}), "ok-val": Variant(Result.Ok, Dict({"value": Int(42)})), "err-val": Variant(Result.Error, Dict({"msg": String("something went wrong")}))})
